{"id": "EUVD-2026-86094", "enisaUuid": "16d36e3a-f55a-3dda-b077-c31f6cdf3328", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Fix OOB memory exposure in get_wave_state()\n\nThe get_wave_state() function for v9 trusts cp_hqd_cntl_stack_size and\ncp_hqd_cntl_stack_offset values read directly from the MQD, which are\nwritten by GPU microcode and fully attacker-controlled on the\nCRIU-restore path (via AMDKFD_IOC_RESTORE_PROCESS with H3).\n\nthis leads to an unbounded copy_to_user() that can leak adjacent\nGTT/kernel memory. If offset > size, integer underflow produces a ~4 GiB\nread length, if size is set to 1 MiB against a 4 KiB allocation, we leak\n1 MiB of adjacent kernel memory (other queues' MQDs, ring buffers, KASLR\npointers).\n\nFix by clamping both cp_hqd_cntl_stack_size to the actual allocated\nbuffer size (q->ctl_stack_size) and cp_hqd_cntl_stack_offset to the\nclamped size before performing arithmetic and copy_to_user().\n\nThis ensures we never read beyond the allocated kernel BO regardless of\nattacker-supplied MQD field values.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:59", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2bef0f168be46692a6b900916ff5da3771480ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9183d974ddd5f09d029beaf359275ac20d4d5fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec646686613d8ab05b282d1463a7baa49fd6b83b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ef144458f48d5589e36f1b3d83e83db2e5c5ba5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97496", "GHSA-qvg3-fh9p-wjpx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01537ecd-af0e-3391-9906-73d19131d5ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "06f39d82-3cac-3692-840b-df09fb1c9976", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42c6c48214b726c30918e8dc80e2168607d13ae4 <ec646686613d8ab05b282d1463a7baa49fd6b83b"}, {"id": "17ff1193-dd3f-324d-88c5-d1501f04e2d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42c6c48214b726c30918e8dc80e2168607d13ae4 <7ef144458f48d5589e36f1b3d83e83db2e5c5ba5"}, {"id": "7896a4a4-1842-3562-89b5-29d2fc4d9276", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "85900b10-d07d-3426-a9c0-d09665fdd1fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "892e3050-8c55-3a58-8c0c-fca320986523", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42c6c48214b726c30918e8dc80e2168607d13ae4 <e2bef0f168be46692a6b900916ff5da3771480ed"}, {"id": "8f0c504c-ad94-3a4e-868f-258b6236bb9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "9ef27c8a-3c69-3db7-8bb9-afff5d00ed3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42c6c48214b726c30918e8dc80e2168607d13ae4 <d9183d974ddd5f09d029beaf359275ac20d4d5fe"}, {"id": "e02ff7a1-a3b3-3561-8270-d8aadc21ec6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.18"}, {"id": "f70d2c30-89f3-375a-b05c-df35e9077b76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "51825759-880f-35b4-9d24-24c2b26bb44b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}